Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 19:34:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH v6] selftests/microblaze: add kernel-entry ABI regression test

Add a MicroBlaze selftest that asserts the property the entry.S argument
save-area fix restores: a syscall does not change the user stack pointer.

The MicroBlaze ABI lets a callee spill its incoming argument registers to
the caller-reserved area at [caller_sp + 4, caller_sp + 28).  When entry.S
calls a syscall handler with r1 still at the pt_regs base, that spill area
aliases pt_regs + 4 =3D=3D PT_R1, the saved user stack pointer, so a handler
that spills its first argument overwrites the SP userspace resumes with.
A GCC 15 register-allocation change made such spills common and the bug
fatal (init died with AT_FDCWD as its stack pointer).

The test issues a raw syscall and reads r1 immediately before and after
the "brki r14, 8" trap in one asm block, so the compiler cannot interpose
stack motion; a fixed kernel returns identical values, a regressed kernel
differs.  It is skipped on non-MicroBlaze builds.

Signed-off-by: Sam Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
